      },
      {
        "id": "s3_construction",
        "kind": "text",
        "label": "Construction",
        "marks": 1,
        "mark_note": "Construction",
        "margin_note": "Name every point you drew. The examiner matches these names against the figure.",
        "lines": [
          {
            "text": "Construction:",
            "style": "heading"
          },
          "Let OA = P and OB = Q act at the point O,",
          "with ∠AOB = θ.",
          "Complete the parallelogram OACB.",
          "Join OC. The diagonal OC = R is the resultant.",
          "Draw CD ⊥ to OA extended, meeting it at D.",
          "Let ∠AOC = α."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "s4_legs",
        "kind": "equation",
        "label": "Find AD and CD",
        "marks": 1,
        "mark_note": "Triangle CAD",
        "margin_note": "AC is parallel to OB, so the angle at A equals θ. Both legs come from this one triangle.",
        "lines": [
          "In the right triangle CAD:",
          {
            "text": "∠CAD = θ   (AC is parallel to OB)",
            "style": "eq"
          },
          {
            "text": "AD = Q cos θ",
            "style": "eq"
          },
          {
            "text": "CD = Q sin θ",
            "style": "eq"
          },
          {
            "text": "∴ OD = OA + AD = P + Q cos θ",
            "style": "eq"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "s5_pythagoras",
        "kind": "equation",
        "label": "Apply Pythagoras",
        "marks": 1,
        "mark_note": "Magnitude",
        "margin_note": "Show the expansion and the sin²θ + cos²θ = 1 step. Skipping it loses the mark.",
        "lines": [
          "In the right triangle ODC:",
          {
            "text": "OC² = OD² + CD²",
            "style": "eq"
          },
          {
            "text": "R² = (P + Q cos θ)² + (Q sin θ)²",
            "style": "eq"
          },
          {
            "text": "R² = P² + 2PQ cos θ + Q²cos²θ + Q²sin²θ",
            "style": "eq"
          },
          {
            "text": "R² = P² + Q² + 2PQ cos θ  (∵ sin²θ + cos²θ = 1)",
            "style": "eq"
          },
          {
            "text": "R = √(P² + Q² + 2PQ cos θ)",
            "style": "boxed"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "s6_direction",
        "kind": "equation",
        "label": "Direction of R",
        "marks": 1,
        "mark_note": "tan α",
        "margin_note": "Use the same right triangle ODC. Say which side is opposite and which is adjacent to α.",
        "lines": [
          "Direction: in the right triangle ODC,",
          {
            "text": "tan α = CD / OD",
            "style": "eq"
          },
          {
            "text": "tan α = Q sin θ / (P + Q cos θ)",
            "style": "eq"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "s7_alpha",
        "kind": "boxed_final",
        "label": "Final answer for α",
        "marks": 1,
        "mark_note": "Direction",
        "margin_note": "Box both final answers. The examiner finds them in one glance.",
        "lines": [
          "The angle α gives the direction of R with P.",
          {
            "text": "∴ α = tan⁻¹ [ Q sin θ / (P + Q cos θ) ]",
            "style": "boxed"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "s8_special_cases",
        "kind": "text",
        "label": "Special cases (extra)",
        "marks": 0,
        "margin_note": "Not asked. Write it only if time is left.",
        "lines": [
          {
            "text": "Special cases:",
            "style": "heading"
          },
          {
            "text": "θ = 0°  → R = P + Q  (maximum)",
            "style": "indent"
          },
          {
            "text": "θ = 90° → R = √(P² + Q²)",
            "style": "indent"
          },
          {
            "text": "θ = 180° → R = P − Q  (minimum)",
            "style": "indent"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
